{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04P0", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{descent-section-fpqc-universal-effective-epimorphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:75a59a20f0664c1f0bd94e7a18f5ffbc59124f7268b36c705c29ecc7ab83b3cd", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis section is the analogue of\nDescent, Section <REF_0001>.\nAt the moment we do not know if all of the material for\nfpqc coverings of schemes holds also for algebraic spaces.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:95a74750c12c7b22ac8786dab3735291ddad8a6f6ac52ae43e6a8641cb8e50f6", "unit_id": "tag:04P0:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04P0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{f_i : T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$i$", "MATH_0005": "$W_i \\subset T_i$", "MATH_0006": "$i, j \\in I$", "MATH_0007": "$\\text{pr}_0^{-1}(W_i) = \\text{pr}_1^{-1}(W_j)$", "MATH_0008": "$T_i \\times_T T_j$", "MATH_0009": "$W \\subset T$", "MATH_0010": "$W_i = f_i^{-1}(W)$", "MATH_0011": "$i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-open-fpqc-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fe6d542b6a47ecce3199f6db9d70b9effa256e95403a2122b49e371a0b67f864", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:16b3c0b3bb99d875e8ee7d742ed68ef6a84443ced4f7862c2f2e6546d223c2b4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an fpqc covering\nof algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\nSuppose that for each <MATH_0004> we have an open subspace <MATH_0005>\nsuch that for all <MATH_0006> we have\n<MATH_0007> as open\nsubspaces of <MATH_0008>. Then there exists a unique open subspace\n<MATH_0009> such that <MATH_0010> for each <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f1635d7b7653276b4a2048c813ec0e16e85620d74b51175830b51380ff3c389a", "unit_id": "tag:04P1:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04P0", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$T_i$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\to T$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{T_i \\times_T U \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$T_i \\times_T U$", "MATH_0007": "$i$", "MATH_0008": "$W_i \\times_T U$", "MATH_0009": "$W' \\subset U$", "MATH_0010": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0011": "$W \\subset X$", "MATH_0012": "$W'$", "MATH_0013": "$W_i$", "MATH_0014": "$W$", "MATH_0015": "$i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-topologies-lemma-refine-fpqc-schemes}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{descent-lemma-open-fpqc-covering}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-properties-section-points}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0dea1d981250b76b1ca232f9fb90e59c9436e6314122792d07294399c3844e55", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:830c205288765b3807bf4a935ced47d1f358d6240bd9ec221e7ef9ec3c9f4b08", "source_text": "By\nTopologies on Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe may assume each <MATH_0001> is a scheme.\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0002> and a surjective <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism <MATH_0003>.\nThen <MATH_0004> is an fpqc covering of <MATH_0005>\nand <MATH_0006> is a scheme for each <MATH_0007>. Hence we\nsee that the collection of opens <MATH_0008> comes from a unique\nopen subscheme <MATH_0009> by\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nAs <MATH_0010> is open we can define <MATH_0011> the Zariski\nopen which is the image of <MATH_0012>, see\nProperties of Spaces, Section <REF_0003>.\nWe omit the verification that this works, i.e., that\n<MATH_0013> is the inverse image of <MATH_0014> for each <MATH_0015>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4b40305f27f5704abb6edc77bb9baacf6e59899ffc5b7a3d27094391975b8eb5", "unit_id": "tag:04P1:proof"}
